liance with the literal access precondition. A healthy permitted execution prefix and successful response can coexist with the observed ordering violation.',['Only method order is checked; transport-error handling, request correlation under faults and consensus effects remain independent.'])\nitem('checker_correspondence','Inspected fixed plan.json and assurance_generated_test.go for artifact 6ac27453c3ba4c08ac32729d6b783b1b and raw execution 59614562669b48149511f09b7690de2d. NewRaft, bootstrap, AddVoter and Apply run actual workers. The wrapper maps each concrete AppendFuture pointer to a unique observational wrapper for both AppendEntries return and Consumer delivery; the producer retains its own original future and completes it with respond, not Error. Consumer forwarding preserves order. The observed Error method delegates and records return; Response records that per-object flag before delegating the real getter. pipelineDecode performs these accesses in its decoder goroutine, so the atomic flag is not an invented response property. A single CAS selects the first actual Response independently of the flag, avoiding selection by failing outcome. The event response_invoked admits this operation; response_returned records actual underlying getter completion and the saved entry-time flag. Stable history/operation identifiers correlate exactly one pair. Raw events show term 2, previous index 4, zero entries, error_returned_before_call=false, followed by a real successful term-2 response and driver_complete after Apply. Empty entries do not exempt the future method contract. The oracle compares only the false flag with required true; it does not label successful response data as bad or claim a match index was advanced. The source has no Error call in pipelineDecode; wrappers do not suppress one. Shutdown runs independently and the execution completed without timeout. Underlying completion before the wrapper itself returns is sufficient here because the prohibited acce